                <pb facs="0623" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg525"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1336.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the last paragraph of my
                    dispatch No. 1319, of the 26th ultimo, I have the honor to inform you of the
                    receipt to-day of a formal note from the imperial foreign office, expressing the
                    thanks of the German Government for the friendly offer made by Lady Randolph
                    Churchill, the chairman of the committee of the American hospital ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, to receive wounded German soldiers and
                    sailors on board the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, and stating that the
                    authorities concerned have been duly notified.</p>
                <p>I shall communicate this information to the committee in London.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
